## Fix Verification Protocol
When implementing fixes for reported issues, ALL of the following apply:
- **User intent overrides guide defaults.** If a user specifies a glyph, label, or behaviour for a specific element, use exactly that — do not substitute the guide's categorical default.
- **Every discrete complaint clause maps to a discrete code change.** Broad to-dos that group multiple complaint sentences are insufficient. Track each sentence.
- **No complaint clause may be skipped** in favour of easier clauses. Structural fixes (architecture, lifecycle, overlay) are not deferrable.
- **Data dependencies must be fulfilled.** If code reads a field (e.g. `entry.description`), that field must exist in the data source. Code that reads an absent field is not a fix.
- **Post-fix verification is mandatory.** After all changes: re-read the original complaint sentence by sentence. For each clause, confirm a code change (file + method + value) exists. If any clause has no corresponding change, the work is incomplete — do not mark done.

